":"__P27#","2121":"__P7E#"},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Waters, which in that country are very scarce. — Milk. Septuagint, “fat.” (Calmet) — In the western Churches, wine and honey were given to the new baptized, chap. vii. 15. (St. Jerome) — Christ invites all to come to him, John iv. 14,. and vii. 37. The establishment of the Church is described under the figure of the return from Babylon. (Calmet) — Grace is offered to all. But only those are justified who thirst, and do their best, Matthew v. 6. (Worthington)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","David. I will be equally faithful to you, Psalm lxxxviii. 29. Septuagint, “the holy things of David faithful,” Acts xiii. 34. The resurrection of Christ fully accomplished the promise made to David."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Him. David, who continually proclaimed the divine mercies, (Psalm xvii. 1.) or rather Christ; though Grotius alone would refer it to Jeremias. (Calmet)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Not with approbation. (Haydock) — The Gentiles are converted."],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Near. He will shortly (Calmet) turn to the Gentiles, John xii. 35., and Acts xiii. 46. (Haydock)"],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Way. This is a necessary preliminary to God’s service. (Worthington)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","My ways. I am not vindictive, but require a sincere conversion. (Calmet) — We cannot serve both God and the world. We must therefore adhere to the former. (Worthington)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Sent it. I will assuredly bring you from Babylon; and the rain shall sooner return upwards than I will break my promise."],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Peace, by strangers, chap. xlix. 22. — Hands, for joy. (Calmet) — Ipsa sonant arbusta Deus Deus ille, Menacla. (Virgil, Eclogues v.)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Myrtle-tree. Instead of the wicked, the just shall be seen. (Chaldean) — Away. The conversion and sanctity of the Gentiles shall be a trophy to the Lord. (Menochius)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}